# Session Audit reports are local-only artifacts.
#
# They quote session transcripts, absolute paths, cost accounting, and — because
# memory injection is one of the things they audit — observations that bled in
# from unrelated projects. This repository is public. Concept issue #58 already
# records that these reports are excluded from the tracker for that reason and
# points at this file; the file itself was never committed, so the exclusion it
# assumed was not in force.
#
# To share a finding, quote it into the relevant issue after reading it. Do not
# commit a report wholesale. To keep one deliberately, force-add it only after a
# human privacy review of that specific file.

*.md
*.json
!.gitignore
